  {
   "id": 508723,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Factor: <span data-math=\"{x^2} - 16x + 63\">{x^2} - 16x + 63</span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"{x^2} - 16x + 63\"></span></p>\n<p>Look for factors of 63 that add up to <span data-math=\"-16\"></span>. This works when the coefficient of the <span data-math=\"{x^2}\"></span> term is 1.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Factors of 63</td>\n<td>Sum of Factors = –16</td>\n<td>Success?</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1 times 63</td>\n<td><span data-math=\"1 + 63 = 64\"></span></td>\n<td>No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3 times 21</td>\n<td><span data-math=\"3 + 21 = 24\"></span></td>\n<td>No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>7 times 9</td>\n<td><span data-math=\"7 + 9 = 16\"></span></td>\n<td>No, but it’s the opposite of the sum you want. Try negatives of your factors.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>–7 times –9</td>\n<td><span data-math=\"-7 + \\left({-9} \\right) = -16\"></span></td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Because –7 and –9 are factors of 63 and they add up to –16, you can make the factors of the polynomial.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"(x - 7)(x - 9)\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\left( {x - 7} \\right)\\left( {x - 9} \\right)\">\\left( {x - 7} \\right)\\left( {x - 9} \\right)</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
